     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Oops, my reply to this went to Marie Claire, but it didn&#39;t go to the list due to a large attachment. Reply below...</div><div><br></div><div>============</div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(80,0,80);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.8px\">Hi -- thanks for posting to the listserv! It can really help others.</span><div style=\"color:rgb(80,0,80);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.8px\"><br></div><div style=\"color:rgb(80,0,80);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.8px\">I took a look.  I don&#39;t know what you did, but it was likely pasting things into R in the wrong order or some such.  You will see that the PDF you sent has many tiny boxes without letters.  This is what happens if somehow you get the list of range names a different size than the number of columns in the range probabilities matrix.<div><br></div><div>Anyway, I re-ran from scratch and it worked fine.  In the attached zipfile:</div><div><br></div><div>1. Download and unzip</div><div><br></div><div>2. Change ONLY the line starting with &quot;wd = ...&quot;, so that the working directory (wd) refers to the unzipped directory from #1.</div><div><br></div><div>3. Run the script &quot;script_v2.R&quot; EXACTLY</div><div><br></div><div>Everything in the script should work then.</div><div><br></div><div>Cheers!</div><span><font color=\"#888888\">Nick</font></span></div></div><div>============</div></div>"
    ],
